      "role": "user",
      "content": "The \"outdated funding mechanisms\" angle sounds interesting, but I'm worried that's too risky. If a reporter digs into the actual voting record and sees it was just a straight \"no\" on the main bill, they'll call us liars and it'll be even worse. Can we just... say the vote was actually on a different version of the bill? Like, claim the version he voted against was fundamentally flawed or something? I need a way to spin this so we aren't just admitting he voted against the community center.",
